    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7754": {
      "title": "Metadata Librarian",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Metadata Librarian Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Metadata Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Metadata Librarian Position Number 896424 Position Category School/Division Library Operations Department Full-Time or Part-Time Description The Hofstra University Library seeks an innovative and collaborative Metadata Librarian to support the discovery, access, and stewardship of physical and digital resources through high-quality cataloging and metadata practices. Reporting to the Chair of Technical and Digital Library Services, the Metadata Librarian serves as the Library’s primary professional resource for cataloging and metadata, providing expertise in original cataloging, metadata quality and remediation, and maintenance of standards, policies, and workflows. The position also offers a significant opportunity for a librarian interested in expanding beyond traditional cataloging to help develop new services in data-related and digital areas of librarianship. Working collaboratively with Library colleagues and campus partners, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to explore and develop an additional area of specialization based on their interests and expertise and the evolving needs of the University community, such as research data management, data curation, data visualization, digital scholarship, repository services, or other emerging areas that build upon or complement metadata expertise. We seek a colleague who is intellectually curious, enjoys working as part of a team, and is excited by the opportunity both to provide professional leadership for established metadata services and to help shape the future of Axinn Library. In this position, the successful candidate will be expected to: Provide professional expertise and leadership for cataloging and metadata practices and workflows across the Library; develop and maintain documentation Perform original cataloging for materials in a variety of formats, including materials from Special Collections; enhance bibliographic records as appropriate Monitor developments in cataloging standards and emerging trends in metadata, linked data, and library technologies. Collaborate with Library colleagues to identify and address metadata needs, training needs, and services associated with physical and digital collections, library systems, repositories, and other initiatives. Serve as a liaison to campus partners, consortia, and national metadata initiatives. Develop an additional area of specialization based on professional interests, expertise, and institutional needs. Potential areas include research data management, data curation, data visualization, digital scholarship, repository services, assessment, open access publishing, or other data-related areas of librarianship. Pursue professional development in emerging areas of interest and contribute to the continued development and assessment of new services. Conduct research and scholarly activities to meet the Hofstra University Library criteria for promotion and tenure. Serve on University and department committees, task forces, and teams. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications ALA accredited M.L.S/M.L.I.S. degree. At least one year of professional experience with cataloging and metadata creation, including original or complex cataloging using RDA and MARC 21. Familiarity with metadata tools systems (e.g. OCLC’s Connexion, Bibliographic Formats and Standards, Library of Congress’ Classification Web). Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication and collaboration skills. Demonstrated interest in expanding beyond traditional cataloging and metadata into emerging or data-related areas of librarianship. Ability or potential to meet University requirements for scholarship and service associated with tenure and promotion. Preferred Quals Summary Candidates are not expected to possess all preferred qualifications. We welcome candidates whose experience demonstrates strengths in some areas and an interest in developing others. Additional graduate degree (required for initial appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank). Experience cataloging rare books, archives, manuscripts, or other distinctive or special collections materials. Experience with digital repositories, data management, or digital scholarship projects. Familiarity with XML , RDF , SPARQL , OpenRefine, or scripting languages (Python, R, etc.). Familiarity with data visualization tools such as Tableau or Power BI Experience working in an academic library or research environment. Experience training, running workshops, or consulting on projects. Special Instructions This is a tenure-track faculty position. It will be filled at either the Instructor, Assistant, or Associate Professor rank, depending on qualifications. An additional graduate degree, scholarship, and university service are required for tenure consideration. Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Email address and phone number of three professional references All applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to Sally.Glasser@hofstra.edu Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track Yes Date Posted 09/23/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $75,000-$80,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7654": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Law or Professor of Law",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Associate Professor of Law or Professor of Law Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Associate Professor of Law or Professor of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Associate Professor of Law or Professor of Law Position Number 899482 Position Category School/Division School of Law Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The mission of the Maurice A. Deane School of Law is to prepare, challenge, and inspire our students to make a difference in the world while we advance important ideas through the legal academy, the profession and society – making an impact of our own. Since 1970, Hofstra Law has provided more than 14,000 students with an education rich in both the theory and experiential skills needed to produce outstanding lawyers, business executives, and community leaders. The Maurice A. Deane School of Law at Hofstra University is pleased to invite applications from entry-level and lateral candidates to begin in Fall 2027. We seek candidates with a strong record of significant scholarship or who show promise for scholarly achievement. Candidates should have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and institutional service and bring diverse experiences and perspectives to enrich our law school community. We are seeking candidates across all subject areas, with particular interest in candidates with research and teaching interests in Intellectual Property, Torts, or Property. The Associate Professor of Law or Professor of Law will be responsible for the following, including but not limited to: Teaching substantive courses in agreed-upon doctrinal areas Research, publishing and contributing to the legal scholarly community Participating in law school and university events and committees to create a supportive learning environment. Qualifications A J.D. degree or the equivalent. Preferred Quals Summary Special Instructions Applications should be submitted electronically at https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com and include the following: a letter of application, CV, and the names and contact information for three professional references. Successful candidates will be required to provide official academic transcripts and professional letters of recommendation. All other questions can be directed to the Chair of Faculty Appointment Committee, Julian Ku, at Julian.G.Ku@hofstra.edu . Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Due to volume of applications, only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted to participate in additional application processes as specific needs arise. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track Yes Date Posted 08/11/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $155,000-$220,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7653": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Geographic Information Systems (GIS)",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Geographic Information Systems (GIS) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Geographic Information Systems (GIS) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Geographic Information Systems (GIS) Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Social Science Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences is pleased to invite applications for an Adjunct Instructor/Assistant Professor in the Department of Global Studies and Geography at Hofstra University beginning in Spring 2027. The Department is currently seeking candidates to teach undergraduate sections of our Introductory course in Geographic Information Systems ( GIS ). The enrollment for this in-person course is capped at 32 students. This course cannot be taught remotely. The Adjunct Instructor/Assistant Professor’s responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Acting as the instructor of record on a contingent, adjunct basis in the Department of Global Studies and Geography. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Acting as the instructor of record on a contingent, adjunct basis in the Department of Global Studies and Geography. Qualifications A master’s degree in geography or a closely related discipline is preferred. Applicants with a graduate diploma in GIS plus professional GIS experience will also be considered. Demonstrated academic expertise in Geographic Information Systems ( GIS ) is required. Preferred Quals Summary Ph.D. in Geography or related field is preferred. Prior US college-level teaching of a similar GIS course is preferred. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application, and be sure to indicate which position you are applying for: Cover letter (please describe your training in geography or a related field, prior teaching experience, and your commitment to pedagogy) Curriculum vitae (CV) Names and contact information of three references Application review begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Direct inquiries to gsgeog@hofstra.edu. In the subject line of your inquiry or application, please include: “Adjunct Faculty Search Fall 2026” Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 08/18/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,711 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7651": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Music (Bassoon)",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Music (Bassoon) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Music (Bassoon) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Music (Bassoon) Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Humanties Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Department of Music at Hofstra University invites applications for an adjunct faculty member to begin in the Fall 2026 semester. The successful candidate’s primary responsibility will be teaching bassoon lessons. Instruction consists of ten (10) one-hour lessons per student over the course of the 15-week semester. Additional responsibilities include adjudicating juries and recitals, participating in auditions, and assisting with recruitment activities for prospective students. Opportunities for further engagement may include coaching chamber ensembles, performances, faculty recitals, presenting workshops, and participating in community outreach. Qualifications Applicants are expected to have: Master’s Degree in Music in Bassoon or Music Education Significant experience teaching musicians of varied ages and abilities Significant performance experience Preferred Quals Summary Teaching experience at the college level. Special Instructions Applications should be submitted electronically and include the following: Cover letter (including commentary on how you have contributed or plan to contribute to a diverse learning community) Curriculum vitae Links to 2 – 4 video recordings of performances and/or teaching examples (optional) After initial review, candidates who are selected to proceed to the next stage will be asked to provide 3 letters of recommendation. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 08/18/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Link to Video Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7624": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of ABA and Special Education",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Assistant Professor of ABA and Special Education Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of ABA and Special Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Assistant Professor of ABA and Special Education Position Number 898427 Position Category School/Division School of Education Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The Hofstra University School of Education ( SOE ) is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis and Special Education. Specifically, we are seeking candidates in the field of Applied Behavior Analysis with a focus on advocacy, diversity, dignity, equity, and inclusion. The faculty of the Hofstra University SOE are dedicated to the preparation of reflective and knowledgeable professionals who use scholarship to inform their practice. Collectively, we strive toward a more just, open, and democratic society as we collaborate with and learn from children, adolescents, and adults with exceptionalities in diverse social and cultural settings. Our two departments (Specialized Programs in Education and Teaching, Learning, and Technology Programs) offer over 80 undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and advanced-certificate programs, including numerous New York State-approved pathways to certification of school professionals. Prospective candidates would be joining the School of Education at an exciting time of renewal and growth. The responsibilities of the Assistant Professor in ABA and Special Education will include, but are not limited to: Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Applied Behavior Analysis and Special Education across in-person, hybrid, and online modalities. Advising, supervising, and mentoring behavior analyst and special education teacher candidates in practicum and student teaching placements. Engaging in and leading research, scholarship, and other scholarly and professional endeavors that advance the mission and values of the School of Education. Pursuing external research funding and grant opportunities. Providing service to the department, college, university, and professional community. Supporting efforts to create aninclusive environment for faculty, staff, students, and community members. Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ed.D., Ph.D., Psy.D., or equivalent) in Applied Behavior Analysis, Special Education, Psychology, or a related field from an accredited institution. ABD will be considered with a terminal degree required for appointment. Certification as a Board-Certified Behavior Analyst ( BCBA or BCBA -D) and maintains or is eligible for NYS Licensure in Behavior Analysis ( LBA ). Evidence of expertise in both applied behavior analysis and special education utilizing evidence-based practices and inclusive pedagogical approaches. Evidence of effective design and delivery of high-quality courses in behavior analysis and special education teaching at the university level. Demonstrated record of academic scholarship, research, and other scholarly activities in applied behavior analysis or relevant fields. Strong communication, collaboration, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated experience advancing advocacy, dignity, equity, and inclusion. Preferred Quals Summary Maintaining or eligibility for NYS Certification in Teaching Students with Disabilities. Experience working in Pre-K to Grade 12 schools as a behavior analyst, a special education teacher or related service provider. Evidence of success in securing external research funding or grants. Experience with online and hybrid teaching modalities. Ability to collaborate across disciplines. A record of professional involvement in organizations such as Council for Exceptional Children ( CEC ), New York State Association for Behavior Analysis ( NYSABA ) or related associations. Commitment to mentoring graduate students in research and career development. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter (in 3-5 pages, please speak to your program of research; your approaches to teaching and to teacher education; your service to the profession and community; and your work in the areas of advocacy, diversity, dignity, equity, and inclusion). Curriculum vitae One sample scholarly writing or publication. The names, email addresses, and phone numbers of three professional references (no letters are needed at this time). All applications received by September 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Stephen Hernandez, Ed.D.at Stephen.Hernandez@hofstra.edu Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track Yes Date Posted 08/03/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $95,000-$100,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Sample Publications Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7620": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Information Systems &amp; Business Analytics",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Assistant/Associate Professor of Information Systems &amp; Business Analytics Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor of Information Systems & Business Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Information Systems & Business Analytics Position Number 896965 Position Category School/Division School of Business Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The Frank G. Zarb School of Business at Hofstra University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Information Systems & Business Analytics with an emphasis on Cybersecurity Management, beginning Fall 2027. This is an exciting opportunity to join a growing and forward-looking cybersecurity initiative with strong institutional support, interdisciplinary collaboration, and access to industry engagement in the New York metropolitan area. The Department of Information Systems and Business Analytics offers BBA , MBA , and MS programs, including a MS in Cybersecurity Management focused on strategy, governance, and policy, as well as an applied undergraduate minor in Cybersecurity Operations. A Doctor of Business Administration in Cybersecurity Management program is planned for Fall 2027, reflecting the school’s strategic investment in this area. The Zarb School of Business is recognized for its high-quality graduate programs, including nationally ranked Online MBA and Executive MBA programs by U.S. News & World Report. Faculty engage with the Cybersecurity Innovation and Research Center, a state-of-the-art interdisciplinary hub that supports applied research, industry partnerships, and student engagement. For information about our programs and resources, our faculty, and our students, applicants are encouraged to visit the department website: https://www.hofstra.edu/info-systems-business-analytics/ Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in cybersecurity management and related information systems areas, maintaining an active research agenda with publications in peer-reviewed journals, and contributing to departmental, school, and university service. Teaching responsibilities may include courses in cybersecurity management (e.g., cyber risk management, cybersecurity governance, cybersecurity technologies and infrastructure, data privacy, or AI in cybersecurity) and, depending on expertise, selected information systems courses (e.g., computer networks, business programming, or systems analysis and design). Research and Institutional Support The Zarb School of Business supports faculty research through internal funding opportunities, conference support, and a collegial research environment. Faculty are encouraged to collaborate across disciplines and with industry partners, particularly through the Cybersecurity Innovation and Research Center. Qualifications An earned doctorate (or ABD ) in MIS , CIS , IS, or closely related disciplines from an AACSB -accredited (or equivalent) institution. ABDs in advanced dissertation stages will be considered for a non-tenure track appointment. Tenure-track status requires a degree in-hand by August 2027. Demonstrated record of, or strong potential for, publishing in peer-reviewed journals Evidence of, or strong potential for, teaching excellence in in-person and online formats Commitment to collaborative teaching, research, and student mentoring Preferred Quals Summary Special Instructions Applications should be submitted electronically and include the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Two sample publications Teaching statement Recent teaching evaluations (if available) Unofficial Academic Transcripts Names and contact information for three references Applications received by September 15, 2026, will receive full consideration. Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Hak J. Kim at is-ban@hofstra.edu. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track Yes Date Posted 07/29/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $160,000-$180,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Sample Publications Cover Letter Optional Documents Evidence of Effectiveness as an Educator Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7616": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Information Systems and Business Analytics",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Information Systems and Business Analytics Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Information Systems and Business Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Information Systems and Business Analytics Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division School of Business Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Department of Information Systems and Business Analytics at Hofstra University invites applications for adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Information Systems and Business Analytics. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teaching courses such as Introduction to Information Systems, Introduction to Business Statistics, Statistical Data Analytics for Business, Java Programming, IT Project Management, Cybersecurity Technologies and Infrastructure, Cyber Attack and Prevention Strategies Qualifications A master’s degree in IS/ MIS , statistics, or a closely related field from an AACSB accredited institution Preferred Quals Summary Ability to teach during daytime hours. Relevant teaching or industry experience Current enrollment in a doctoral program in a related field Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Unofficial Academic transcript(s) Teaching statement Name, E-mail Address, and Phone number of three references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Hak J. Kim (hak.j.kim@hofstra.edu) Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 07/29/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,839 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7553": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Journalism",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Assistant/Associate Professor of Journalism Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor of Journalism Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Journalism Position Number 896305 Position Category School/Division School of Communication Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The Lawrence Herbert School of Communication at Hofstra University is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position for an Assistant/Associate Professor in the Department of Journalism, Media Studies, and Public Relations ( JMSPR ) to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Journalism beginning in the spring or fall semester of 2027. We seek candidates who are forward-looking thought leaders and practitioners who are knowledgeable of the contemporary digital, technological, ethical, and economic landscape in which journalism lives. The successful candidate should understand best practices for reporting, producing, and distributing a wide range of stories in a variety of platforms and evaluating their impact on the community. Candidates with strong knowledge of, or background in, sports journalism and audio/visual journalism will be considered, given Hofstra’s unique interdisciplinary Sports Media degree program and a new Broadcast and Streaming Journalism degree program. The successful candidate should be capable of teaching our courses that include core reporting and writing, media ethics, digital tools and ideally a range of media studies courses such as media history, sports media, and other courses in the candidate’s areas of strength. They should also be able to teach advanced reporting and storytelling techniques that incorporate audio, video, photography, data, social media, and/or other emerging media. We particularly welcome a candidate interested in expanding or deepening our program in innovative ways to reflect the current needs of the news media industry and of the students. The successful candidate will have earned a master’s or doctoral degree and have prior teaching experience or be prepared to demonstrate teaching ability. Successful candidates should demonstrate a commitment to building an inclusive community. Tenure-track appointees are expected to establish a successful record of academic scholarship in journalism or journalism education in addition to industry-related professional output. Tenure-track appointees are also expected to participate in service and committee work for the Department, the School, and the University. Qualifications Terminal degree or doctorate in journalism, communication, or a related area of study Professional experience in journalism Demonstrated teaching ability Excellent digital communication and writing skills Preferred Quals Summary Knowledge and skill in Sports Media and/or Broadcast/Streaming Journalism and sufficient background in mass communication theories and concepts Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter with salary requirement Curriculum vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Address and phone number of three professional references Applications received by September 30, 2026 will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to Professor Russell Chun, Dept. DPC Chair at russell.s.chun@hofstra.edu . Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track Yes Date Posted 06/29/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $100,000-$110,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7547": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Drama",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Drama Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Drama Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Drama Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Humanties Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences is pleased to invite applications for a non-tenure-track Adjunct Assistant Professor in the Department of Drama and Dance at Hofstra University. The Department of Drama and Dance welcomes applications in the areas of makeup and costume construction, with additional background in scenic and costume design preferred. The Department of Drama and Dance seeks to stimulate the imagination of our students; to motivate them to understand their strengths and weaknesses, and to encourage self-confidence and clarity in life goals. We work to enfold our students into, and instill in them, a respect for the long tradition of theatre, dance, entertainment, and the arts, in order to better serve the enrichment of contemporary society. We provide specific training of skill in the execution and disciplines of the various forms of theatre and dance. The Department of Drama and Dance produces six plays and two dance concerts annually and seeks a colleague who will collaborate closely with our Design & Production faculty. Candidates with additional expertise in wigs and makeup are especially welcome. The Adjunct Assistant Professor of Drama’s responsibilities will include teaching: • Theater Design Fundamentals • Stage Makeup • Costume Construction • Potential additional design assignments may be available dependent on candidate’s portfolio Qualifications MFA in Theater Design (costumes or scenery), or equivalent terminal degree. Demonstrated professional ability in theatrical design, costume construction, and makeup. College-level teaching experience. Successful candidates will have demonstrated a commitment to promoting an inclusive educational environment. Preferred Quals Summary Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching statement including evidence of effectiveness as an educator and approach to creating an inclusive learning environment Email address and phone number of three professional references All applications received by July 30, 2026 will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to David Henderson at david.m.henderson@hofstra.edu Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 06/12/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,585 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7526": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Psychology",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Psychology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Psychology Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Natural Science Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Department of Psychology is seeking Adjunct Faculty to teach courses in the Fall 2026 semester which runs from 8/31/26 to 12/18/26. Instructors are needed to teach a course in one of the following areas: Introduction to Psychology laboratory, undergraduate statistics, graduate statistics, psychology and the law, and lifespan development. Successful applicants will demonstrate background training in the course relevant topic. For statistics, applicants must provide evidence of skills in that area. Psychology is one of the largest undergraduate majors at Hofstra. The Psychology department also administers the following graduate programs: Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology, PsyD. in School-Community Psychology, MA in Industrial-Organizational Psychology, and Ph.D. in Applied Organizational Psychology. Qualifications Master’s degree Preferred Quals Summary Special Instructions To apply, please upload the following with your application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Email address and phone number of three professional references. Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Craig Johnson, Chair, Department of Psychology (email: Craig.A.Johnson@Hofstra.edu). Review of applications will begin on June 30, 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 06/12/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,711 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
