    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6786": {
      "title": "Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Position Number 999895 Position Category School/Division School of Law Department Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Paralegal Studies Certificate Program at Hofstra Law School seeks a qualified instructor to teach courses in Introduction to Law, Civil Litigation, Family Law, Real Estate Law, Business Organizations, Legal Research and Writing, Immigration Law, Contract Law, Bankruptcy Law, Wills, Trusts & Estates, Criminal Law, and Information Technology for Paralegals. This is an in-person teaching position designed for professionals who are passionate about legal education and committed to preparing students for successful paralegal careers. The program serves adult learners completing an intensive six-month, 306-hour certificate program. The schedule is Monday through Thursday, 9:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. Teach assigned courses in accordance with the program’s approved curriculum and learning outcomes. Deliver engaging, student-centered instruction that integrates legal theory with practical application. Utilize technology, including the Canvas Learning Management System, to post materials, manage assignments, and communicate with students. Evaluate student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback. Maintain accurate attendance, grading, and course documentation. Foster a professional, inclusive, and supportive classroom environment. Participate in faculty meetings and collaborate with the Program Director to ensure course consistency and instructional quality. Qualifications Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an accredited law school. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Quals Summary College or adult education teaching experience. Proficiency in educational technology and learning management systems (preferably Canvas). Practical legal experience in one or more of the following areas: Civil Litigation, Family Law, Real Estate Law, Business Organizations, Legal Research and Writing, Immigration Law, Contract Law, Bankruptcy Law, Wills, Trusts & Estates, Criminal Law, or Information Technology for Paralegals. Special Instructions Applications should be submitted electronically and include the following: A completed application for employment. A cover letter describing teaching experience and areas of legal expertise. A current résumé or curriculum vitae. Contact information for two professional references. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 11/19/2025 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $70 per course hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6739": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Physician Assistant Studies",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Physician Assistant Studies Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Physician Assistant Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Physician Assistant Studies Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra Northwell School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra University’s School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies seeks an Adjunct Clinical Academic Faculty member to teach in the Department of Physician Assistant Studies. Reporting to the Program Director, the adjunct faculty member will provide instruction during the didactic, clinical, and research phases of the PA program across Fall, Spring, and Summer terms. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide dual-degree, didactic year, clinical year, and/or research semester instruction during Fall, Spring, and Summer terms. Instruct and assess students in courses such as physical examination and diagnostic modalities, correlative medicine, structure lab, simulation activities, and summative exams. Proctor examinations and assist with exam administration. Identify students with performance deficiencies and develop strategies to address deficiencies, including remediation exercises. Act as a liaison to core faculty for college resources, textbooks, and teaching materials. Update instructional materials on learning management systems (e.g., Canvas) and ensure course materials are posted in a timely manner. Collaborate with program leadership to enhance curriculum design and maintain compliance with accreditation standards. Perform other related duties as assigned by the Program Director. Qualifications Must hold a current Physician Assistant license in New York State and be NCCPA certified. Minimum of a Master’s degree in Physician Assistant Studies, Public Health, Health Professions Education, or a related field. Demonstrated knowledge of and commitment to the physician assistant profession. Willingness to participate in a collaborative faculty process and contribute to program development. Preferred Quals Summary Previous teaching experience in physician assistant education or clinical instruction. Special Instructions Please upload the following documents with your application for consideration: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement including evidence of effectiveness as an educator and approach to creating an inclusive learning environment. Contact information (email and phone number) for three professional references. All applications received by January 30, 2026, will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to the Department of PA Studies at Scott.Gould@hofstra.edu. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 11/11/2025 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,839 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6629": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, European Studies/Political Science",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, European Studies/Political Science Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, European Studies/Political Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, European Studies/Political Science Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Social Science Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences is pleased to invite applications for an adjunct position in European Studies directed within the Political Science Department. The European Studies Program welcomes applicants with competencies in European thought and rabbinic literature. The European Studies Program is an interdisciplinary program promoting greater understanding of Europe from both the humanities and social sciences. The Office of the Provost can provide specific information about student enrollment with advanced notice. The position requires the teaching of an undergraduate course entitled Ancient Texts, European Minds: Interpretations of the Hebrew Bible Through the Ages. This course surveys European biblical commentators from antiquity to the modern era. The Adjunct Position in European Studies responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Teach Ancient Texts, European Minds: Interpretations of the Hebrew Bible Through the Ages, for undergraduates (3 hours per week) Additional student contact of a minimum of one hour per week for student assistance Qualifications Master’s degree or equivalent in Hebrew Bible and rabbinic literature required. Demonstrated record of teaching. Commitment to fostering an inclusive learning environment and supporting students from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Quals Summary Special Instructions Please submit the following with your application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Contact information of three professional references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to Professor Carolyn Dudek, carolyn.m.dudek@hofstra.edu Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 10/27/2025 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,585 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
