    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6000": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, French",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, French Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, French Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University seeks candidates who will contribute to a supportive climate for students, faculty, and staff. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, French Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Humanties Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences anticipates some opening throughout the 2024/2025 academic year and invites applications for Adjunct Faculty of French in the Department of Romance Languages and Literatures at Hofstra University. The Department of Romance Languages and Literatures welcomes applicants who can teach languages courses in French from beginning level to intermediate level. Classes will meet face to face either on Mondays and Wednesdays or on Tuesdays and Thursdays. Times can range from early morning to late afternoon. The adjunct faculty member’s responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Acting as the instructor of record on a contingent, adjunct basis in the Department of Romance Languages and Literatures for courses in French, from elementary to high intermediate. Teach a range of French-language courses, from elementary to high intermediate levels. Qualifications Master’s degree in French or in a related field. Preferred Quals Summary University-level teaching experience preferred. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Short letter of application Curriculum vitae E-mail address and phone number of three current professional references (Upon appointment, the successful candidate will be required to submit official academic transcripts and three letters of recommendation.) The Department of Romance Languages and Literatures will continue to review applications until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to the departmental e-mail account: RLL@Hofstra.edu. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 09/26/2024 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,422-$1,794 per credit Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
