Spanish from beginning level to intermediate level. Classes will meet face to face either on Mondays and Wednesdays or on Tuesdays and Thursdays. Times can range from early morning to late afternoon. The adjunct faculty member’s responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Acting as the instructor of record on a contingent, adjunct basis in the Department of Romance Languages and Literatures for courses in Spanish, from elementary to high intermediate. Teach a range of Spanish-language courses, from elementary to high intermediate levels. Qualifications Master’s degree in Spanish or in a related field. Preferred Quals Summary University-level teaching experience preferred. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Short letter of application Curriculum vitae E-mail address and phone number of three current professional references (Upon appointment, the successful candidate will be required to submit official academic transcripts and three letters of recommendation.) The Department of Romance Languages and Literatures will continue to review applications until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to the departmental e-mail account: RLL@Hofstra.edu. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 09/26/2024 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,422-$1,794 per credit Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. 